From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 05:43:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 26/29] logging: bound service output and shutdown

Move service stdout writes to one bounded output worker so a stalled collector cannot block runtime threads on the shared stdout lock. Preserve formatter selection, filters and breadcrumb handling, and keep tool stderr synchronous.

Drop records when output capacity is exhausted and summarize losses after recovery without recursively counting lost summaries. Initialize workers before service work and bound each output guard to one second of draining without a synchronous write, flush or join. Apply the same shutdown boundary to the existing optional trace-file buffer.

Keep this independent of native-resident supervision; native diagnostic forwarding relies on this shared output boundary for lifecycle progress. Document adoption, loss semantics and rollback.
